                <pb facs="0684" n="676" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg676"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.981/58: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-09-17T11:00:00+01:00">September 17, 1939—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 17—10:06 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1281. Department’s 522, 16th.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d626-f1"/> I am asking
                    Foreign Office and War Office if any information is available as to welfare and
                    present whereabouts of Davis and staff.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
